	(104476, 117785, 'tatoeba', '彼の丘の上の別荘は、海を見渡している。', 'His villa on the hill commands the sea.'),
	(104477, 75535, 'tatoeba', 'うん。確か使ってない優待券もどこかにあったはず。', 'Yes. I\'m pretty sure there are complimentary tickets that haven\'t been used somewhere.'),
	(104478, 185181, 'tatoeba', '回数券を下さい。', 'May I have coupon tickets?'),
	(104479, 11013833, 'tatoeba', '友だちと合流するのに手間取った。', 'It took me a while to meet up with my friends.'),
	(104480, 75540, 'tatoeba', '「おはようございます。今日は遅かったですね」「うん。ちょっと手間取っちゃって」', '"Good morning. You\'re a bit late today, aren\'t you?" "Yes, I ran into a bit of trouble."'),
	(104481, 170135, 'tatoeba', '昨日、彼女の家を探すのにちょっとばかり手間取った。', 'I had some trouble finding her house yesterday.'),
	(104482, 118753, 'tatoeba', '彼には武力と財力がある。', 'He has swords and purse.'),
	(104483, 97791, 'tatoeba', '彼らはついに武力に訴えた。', 'They finally appeared to arms.'),
	(104484, 2962015, 'tatoeba', '反対派と警察の間で武力衝突が生じた。', 'Violent clashes broke out between the protesters and the police.'),
	(104485, 1335017, 'tatoeba', '彼に頼るな。', 'Don\'t rely on him.'),
	(104486, 12144409, 'tatoeba', '後でこれ頼もっと。', 'I\'ll order this later.'),
	(104487, 10890188, 'tatoeba', '人に頼りすぎるなよ。', 'Don\'t rely too much on others.'),
	(104488, 10677431, 'tatoeba', 'いつでも頼っていいよ。', 'You can always count on us.'),
	(104489, 108036, 'tatoeba', '彼に頼っておけばいい。', 'You can rely on him.'),
	(104490, 9029768, 'tatoeba', '彼に頼ればいいんだよ。', 'You can rely on him.'),
	(104491, 11459535, 'tatoeba', '頼られたかったんだよ。', 'I was just trying to help.'),
	(104492, 102617, 'tatoeba', '彼は他人の援助に頼った。', 'He drew on others for help.'),
	(104493, 121237, 'tatoeba', '反乱は鎮圧された。', 'The revolt was crushed.'),
	(104494, 8916218, 'tatoeba', '暴動は鎮圧された。', 'The riot was put down.'),
	(104495, 176654, 'tatoeba', '軍隊は暴動を簡単に鎮圧した。', 'The troops easily put down the rebellion.'),
	(104496, 102808, 'tatoeba', '彼は草の上に横たわっていた。', 'He was lying on the grass.'),
	(104497, 111007, 'tatoeba', '彼はベンチに横たわっている。', 'He is lying on the bench.'),
	(104498, 4213544, 'tatoeba', '老人が道で横たわって死んでいた。', 'An old man lay dead on the road.'),
	(104499, 8866509, 'tatoeba', 'トムはベッドに横たわり、天井を見つめていた。', 'Tom was lying in bed, staring up at the ceiling.'),
	(104500, 142950, 'tatoeba', '正午に彼らは休憩するために森の中で横たわった。', 'At noon they lay down in a forest to rest.'),
	(104501, 235693, 'tatoeba', '１日中、ベッドに横たわっていたら、うんざりした。', 'I got tired of lying in bed all day.'),
	(104502, 75543, 'tatoeba', '椅子に横たわる私に、歯科衛生士の女性が「はい、お口を開けてください」と言ったのです。', 'The woman dental hygienist said to me, lying down in the chair, "Right, please open your mouth."'),
	(104503, 208106, 'tatoeba', 'その男はじっと横たわっていた。', 'The man lay motionless.'),
	(104504, 13714059, 'tatoeba', '彼は歯科医師です。', 'He is a dentist.'),
	(104505, 236713, 'tatoeba', '彼の職業は歯科医である。', 'He is a dentist by profession.'),
	(104506, 89201, 'tatoeba', '彼女は歯科医を開業している。', 'She practices as a dentist.'),
	(104507, 173557, 'tatoeba', '校門は8時に開く。', 'The gates of the school open at eight.'),
	(104508, 11006116, 'tatoeba', '校門では生徒会が文化祭の飾りつけをしていた。', 'The student council was putting up decorations for the school festival by the school gate.'),
	(104509, 75546, 'tatoeba', '予鈴だ。校門の辺りにいた生徒たちが一斉に足を速める。', 'It\'s the class bell. The pupils that had been around the school gate quickened their steps as one.'),
	(104510, 144185, 'tatoeba', '人々が一斉に走り出した。', 'People started to run all at once.'),
	(104511, 146162, 'tatoeba', '乗客が一斉に乗ってきた。', 'The passengers came on board all at the same time.'),
	(104512, 1116196, 'tatoeba', '皆が一斉に喋っています。', 'Everyone is talking at the same time.'),
	(104513, 186002, 'tatoeba', '我々はふだんより足を速めて歩いた。', 'We walked more quickly than usual.'),
	(104514, 94787, 'tatoeba', '彼女に追いつくために私は歩を速めた。', 'I quickened my steps to catch up with her.'),
	(104515, 191818, 'tatoeba', 'わたしは運転速度を速めて時間の埋め合わせをしなければならない。', 'I must make up for lost time by driving fast.'),
	(104516, 109282, 'tatoeba', '彼は家の周りを見た。', 'He looked about the house.'),
	(104517, 209967, 'tatoeba', 'その事件の早期解決を期待する。', 'We expect an early settlement of the affair.'),
	(104518, 11052311, 'tatoeba', 'トムのお父さんは、早期退職しました。', 'Tom\'s father retired early.'),
	(104519, 141280, 'tatoeba', '戦争の早期終結が我々の熱烈な願いです。', 'It is our ardent hope that the war will end soon.'),
	(104520, 9250736, 'tatoeba', '医者は難題を抱えている。', 'Doctors have a difficult problem.'),
	(104521, 114150, 'tatoeba', '彼は傘を小脇に抱えていた。', 'He was carrying an umbrella under his arm.'),
	(104522, 8816946, 'tatoeba', 'なんかストレスを抱えてるの？', 'Are you under any stress?'),
	(104523, 97624, 'tatoeba', '彼らはみんな腹を抱えて笑った。', 'They were all in convulsions of laughter.'),
	(104524, 1421570, 'tatoeba', '彼女は鞄を小脇に抱えています。', 'She has a bag under her arm.'),
	(104525, 111735, 'tatoeba', '彼はどうしていいのか分からず頭を抱えた。', 'He did not know what to do, and held his head in his hands.'),
	(104526, 213198, 'tatoeba', 'そのことが我々が抱える問題に新しい面を加える。', 'That adds a new dimension to our problem.'),
	(104527, 120727, 'tatoeba', '彼がブリーフケースを脇に抱えてやってくるのが見えた。', 'I saw him coming with his briefcase under his arm.'),
	(104528, 11839588, 'tatoeba', '分厚い本だな。', 'The book is thick.'),
	(104529, 9153054, 'tatoeba', '氷は、その上を歩けるほど分厚かった。', 'The ice was thick enough to walk on.'),
	(104530, 1045065, 'tatoeba', '彼は分厚い眼鏡をかけています。', 'He wears thick glasses.'),
	(104531, 2853016, 'tatoeba', 'トムは分厚い眼鏡をかけている。', 'Tom is wearing thick glasses.'),
	(104532, 75549, 'tatoeba', 'その女の子は、数冊の本を抱えていた。教科書じゃなく、分厚い上製本。', 'The girl was carrying several books, not textbooks but thick hardback books.'),
	(104533, 76721, 'tatoeba', 'コミックマーケット６７にてコピー本販売。無事完売したので製本しました。', 'They were sold as photocopy books in Comic Market 67. We had no problem selling all of them, so we had bound copies made.'),
	(104534, 75551, 'tatoeba', '私の参謀としてついたからには、危機感を持って任にあたって貰わねば困ります。', 'If you\'re with me as a staff officer, then I need you to bring a sense of danger with you to your work.'),
	(104535, 106859, 'tatoeba', '彼は裁判官に任ぜられた。', 'He was raised to the bench.'),
	(104536, 95951, 'tatoeba', '彼をその職に任ずる必要はない。', 'We have no call to appoint him to the post.'),
	(104537, 3496845, 'tatoeba', 'ベッドを整えて。', 'Make your bed.'),
	(104538, 121288, 'tatoeba', '髪を整えないと。', 'I\'ve got to fix my hair.'),
	(104539, 12700726, 'tatoeba', '髪を整えなきゃ。', 'I must arrange my hair.'),
	(104540, 13537465, 'tatoeba', 'マーグは机を整えた。', 'Marg tidied up the desk.'),
	(104541, 144751, 'tatoeba', '身なりを整えなさい。', 'Make yourself presentable.'),
	(104542, 98996, 'tatoeba', '彼は旅支度を整えていた。', 'He was equipped for a trip.'),
	(104543, 125707, 'tatoeba', '墜落に向けて用意は整えられた。', 'We prepared ourselves for the crash.'),
	(104544, 163536, 'tatoeba', '私の姉は毎週、髪を整えてもらう。', 'My sister has her hair done each week.'),
	(104545, 177785, 'tatoeba', '君はすごく根性があるね。', 'You\'ve got a lot of guts.'),
	(104546, 85163, 'tatoeba', '貧乏するとこじき根性がでる。', 'When a man becomes poor, the beggar in him will come out.'),
	(104547, 107800, 'tatoeba', '彼は結構しぶといね。転んでもただでは起きぬ、いい根性しているよ。', 'He\'s a tenacious guy who always manages to come out on top. He\'s the kind of guy who can turn any situation to his advantage.'),
	(104548, 1167794, 'tatoeba', '見せて。', 'Let me see.'),
	(104549, 11075356, 'tatoeba', '金を見せろ。', 'Show me the money.'),
	(104550, 373277, 'tatoeba', '見せてくれ。', 'Let me check it.'),
	(104551, 175189, 'tatoeba', '見せてあげる。', 'Oh, let me show you.'),
	(104552, 10224950, 'tatoeba', '親には見せたの？', 'Did you show it to your parents?'),
	(104553, 148646, 'tatoeba', '手の内を見せるな。', 'Don\'t show them your hand.'),
	(104554, 993659, 'tatoeba', '写真見せてくれる？', 'Can you show me that picture?'),
	(104555, 11469960, 'tatoeba', '見せてもらえますか？', 'Can you let me see it?'),
	(104556, 13260812, 'tatoeba', 'うちの旦那。', 'He is my husband.'),
	(104557, 11875931, 'tatoeba', '旦那様はどこ？', 'Where\'s your husband?'),
	(104558, 103553, 'tatoeba', '彼は人種差別と戦った。', 'He fought against racial discrimination.'),
	(104559, 8966078, 'tatoeba', 'トムは性差別主義者ではない。', 'Tom isn\'t sexist.'),
	(104560, 88721, 'tatoeba', '彼女は女性差別撤廃を主張した。', 'She advocated equal rights for women.'),
	(104561, 75556, 'tatoeba', 'そうじゃない。性差別やら女性蔑視やら、そういうものとは関係なく、男と女は違うんだ。', 'That\'s not what I meant. I\'m not being sexist. Men and women are just different.'),
	(104562, 95910, 'tatoeba', '彼を空港で盛大に見送った。', 'We gave him a royal send-off at the airport.'),
	(104563, 8655541, 'tatoeba', '私は盛大で豪華な結婚式はいらない。', 'I don\'t want a big, fancy wedding.'),
	(104564, 175737, 'tatoeba', '結婚式の後で盛大な披露宴が催された。', 'There was a big reception after the wedding.'),
	(104565, 124963, 'tatoeba', '転ばぬ先の杖。', 'Forewarned is forearmed.'),
	(104566, 142191, 'tatoeba', '赤ん坊はよく転ぶ。', 'Babies often fall down.'),
	(104567, 3241561, 'tatoeba', '転ばないようにね。', 'Be careful not to fall.'),
	(104568, 153094, 'tatoeba', '私は氷の上で転んだ。', 'I fell down on the ice.'),
	(104569, 101911, 'tatoeba', '彼は転んで怪我をした。', 'He got hurt when he fell down.'),
	(104570, 139878, 'tatoeba', '足がもつれて転びそうになった。', 'I tripped and nearly fell.'),
	(104571, 10605070, 'tatoeba', '足元気をつけないと、滑って転んじゃうよ。', 'Watch your step, or you will slip and fall.'),
	(104572, 124344, 'tatoeba', '冬は道路が凍結するので、よく滑って転びます。', 'It is easy to slip and fall during icy winters.'),
	(104573, 75561, 'tatoeba', 'レギュラーになるなら、人一倍頑張らなくっちゃ。', 'If I\'m to become a regular, I have to work twice as hard as the rest.'),
	(104574, 3480351, 'tatoeba', '頑張れ！', 'Hang on!'),
	(104575, 12302058, 'tatoeba', '頑張って。', 'Good luck.'),
	(104576, 11256113, 'tatoeba', '頑張ろう！', 'Let\'s give it our all!'),
	(104577, 12056078, 'tatoeba', '仕事を頑張る。', 'You\'ll do your best.'),
	(104578, 183652, 'tatoeba', '頑張ってみる。', 'I try.'),
	(104579, 4002047, 'tatoeba', '頑張って下さい。', 'Please do your best.'),
	(104580, 3812373, 'tatoeba', '頑張ってください。', 'Please do your best.'),
	(104581, 11508667, 'tatoeba', 'もっと頑張ります。', 'I\'ll try harder.'),
	(104582, 75562, 'tatoeba', 'ハルくんは昔からこうなの、心根は凄く優しいのよ。', 'Haru\'s always been like that; he\'s very kind at heart.'),
	(104583, 10735510, 'tatoeba', '彼女は科を作った。', 'She was flirtatious.'),
	(104584, 2129385, 'tatoeba', 'トムは神経科医です。', 'Tom is a neurologist.'),
	(104585, 2485943, 'tatoeba', 'トムは精神科医をしている。', 'Tom is a psychiatrist.'),
	(104586, 175404, 'tatoeba', '建設工事の第一段階は終わった。', 'The first phase of construction has been completed.'),
	(104587, 205385, 'tatoeba', 'それはまだ実験段階にあります。', 'It is still in the testing stage.'),
	(104588, 85412, 'tatoeba', '百聞は一見に如かず。', 'Seeing is believing.'),
	(104589, 823590, 'tatoeba', '百聞は一見にしかず。', 'To see is to believe.'),
	(104590, 110024, 'tatoeba', '彼は一見ピアニストらしい。', 'He is apparently a pianist.'),
	(104591, 75569, 'tatoeba', '四天王も倒した、クソ長い地下迷宮もクリアした。', 'I\'d defeated the four sub-bosses and got through the damn long underground labyrinth.'),
	(104592, 123237, 'tatoeba', '内閣を倒せ。', 'Down with the Cabinet!'),
	(104593, 4216202, 'tatoeba', '独裁者を倒すのだ！', 'I will overthrow the dictator.'),
	(104594, 199833, 'tatoeba', 'トムは彼を殴り倒した。', 'Tom knocked him down.'),
	(104595, 170837, 'tatoeba', '座席の背を倒してもいいですか。', 'May I put my seat back?'),
	(104596, 10201337, 'tatoeba', '何度殴り倒されても、闘い続けるなんて立派なもんだ。', 'It\'s so admirable how you keep fighting, even when you\'ve been knocked down over and over again.'),
	(104597, 216590, 'tatoeba', 'シート横にあるノブを前に動かし、シートを倒します。', 'Move the knob at the side of the seat forwards, collapse the seat.'),
	(104598, 104364, 'tatoeba', '彼は十字を切った。', 'He crossed himself.'),
	(104599, 123006, 'tatoeba', '尼僧はお祈りをして十字を切った。', 'The nun prayed and crossed herself.'),
	(104600, 498663, 'tatoeba', '四つ角は二つの道が十字に交わった所である。', 'A crossroads is where two roads meet in an X.'),
	(104601, 142576, 'tatoeba', '青空を背景に木々を描く。', 'Paint the trees against the background of the blue sky.'),
	(104602, 6798412, 'tatoeba', '木々を背景に写真を撮る。', 'We take photos with the trees in the background.'),
	(104603, 866789, 'tatoeba', '彼が背景を説明してくれる。', 'He gives a background.'),
	(104604, 75570, 'tatoeba', '十字キーを上へ！するとＢＧＭが変わり、背景は魔王の居城へ・・・。', 'Hit up on the D-pad, and the background music will change as the background itself becomes the Demon King\'s castle....'),
	(104605, 75571, 'tatoeba', '兄が急逝したのは２年前、義姉は一人兄の遺した小さな宝飾店を健気に守ってきた。', 'Since my brother died suddenly two years ago, my sister-in-law has valiantly kept going the small jewellery store he left her.'),
	(104606, 4488416, 'tatoeba', 'メアリーはトムの義姉です。', 'Mary is Tom\'s step-sister.'),
	(104607, 123079, 'tatoeba', '二人の卑劣な男が私から宝飾品を奪って逃走した。', 'Two nasty guys robbed me of my jewels and ran away.'),
	(104608, 78368, 'tatoeba', '理髪店で彼に会った。', 'I met him at the barber\'s.'),
	(104609, 224277, 'tatoeba', 'ここは免税店ですか。', 'Can I buy things here duty-free?'),
	(104610, 75801, 'tatoeba', '彼が直向きに生きるその姿は実に健気です。', 'The single-minded way he gets on with his life is truly admirable.'),
	(104611, 87939, 'tatoeba', '彼女は知らせを冷静に受け止めた。', 'She took the news calmly.'),
	(104612, 11561512, 'tatoeba', '何でもかんでもそう深刻に受け止めるな。', 'Don\'t take everything so seriously.'),
	(104613, 75572, 'tatoeba', '・・・はぁ、どう状況を受け止めればいいのかしら。', '... Aaah, just how am I supposed to cope with this I wonder?'),
	(104614, 9145780, 'tatoeba', '荷物見ててね。', 'Keep an eye on the bags.'),
	(104615, 12074612, 'tatoeba', '荷物が届いた。', 'A package has arrived.'),
	(104616, 6549586, 'tatoeba', '荷物を準備して。', 'Pack your bags.'),
	(104617, 11686087, 'tatoeba', '敵が後方から攻めてきた。', 'The enemy attacked from behind.'),
	(104618, 10854066, 'tatoeba', 'バスの後方へお詰め願います。', 'Please move to the rear of the bus.'),
	(104619, 10906624, 'tatoeba', 'あなたは私を後方へ押し始めた。', 'You started pushing me backwards.'),
	(104620, 75574, 'tatoeba', '後方の敵は現状あくまで退路を断つだけの存在。', 'The enemy behind us presently exists solely to cut off our retreat.'),
	(104621, 96815, 'tatoeba', '彼らは食料の供給を断たれた。', 'They were cut off from food supplies.'),
	(104622, 636242, 'tatoeba', 'それは快刀乱麻を断つような解答でした。', 'That was a \'cutting the Gordian knot\' type of solution.'),
	(104623, 235491, 'tatoeba', '２時間ほど前から雷雨のため連絡が断たれている。', 'Communications have been cut off for two hours because of a thunderstorm.'),
	(104624, 144118, 'tatoeba', '人々は供給が断たれるまでは電気をあって当然のものと思っている。', 'People take electricity for granted until its supply is cut off.'),
	(104625, 233388, 'tatoeba', 'あなたの喫煙習慣を断つ努力をすべきです。', 'You should try to conquer your smoking habit.'),
	(104626, 169157, 'tatoeba', '仕事に応募する。', 'I\'m applying for a job.'),
	(104627, 106604, 'tatoeba', '彼は仕事に応募した。', 'He applied for a job.'),
	(104628, 112663, 'tatoeba', '彼はその奨学金に応募した。', 'He applied for the scholarship.'),
	(104629, 11030776, 'tatoeba', '意外と面白い組み合わせかもね。', 'It may be an unexpectedly interesting combination.'),
	(104630, 11014051, 'tatoeba', 'トーナメントの組み合わせを見たら、みんな無言になった。', 'Everyone fell silent when they saw the tournament matchups.'),
	(104631, 190611, 'tatoeba', '一国にとって金融政策と財政政策の適切な組み合わせが大切である。', 'It is important for a nation to have an adequate mix of monetary and fiscal policies.'),
	(104632, 2226639, 'tatoeba', '彼は愚かだ。', 'He is foolish.'),
	(104633, 232111, 'tatoeba', 'あなたは愚かだ。', 'You are stupid.'),
	(104634, 10824397, 'tatoeba', '人間って愚かね。', 'Humans are silly.'),
	(104635, 11571571, 'tatoeba', 'それは豆腐よ。', 'That\'s tofu.'),
	(104636, 8534154, 'tatoeba', '豆腐を食べます。', 'I eat tofu.'),
	(104637, 11052333, 'tatoeba', '豆腐は好きですか？', 'Do you like tofu?'),
	(104638, 75582, 'tatoeba', '豆腐は軽く重しをして、２０分ほどおいて水切りする。', 'Lightly weigh the tofu down, leave it for about 20 minutes then drain.'),
	(104639, 10118358, 'tatoeba', 'トムは池で水切りをしてた。', 'Tom was skipping rocks on the pond.'),
	(104640, 75583, 'tatoeba', 'ウチは俗に言うシングルマザーの家庭だ。父親の顔を僕は知らない。', 'We\'re what they colloquially call a single mother family. I haven\'t seen my father\'s face.'),
	(104641, 177901, 'tatoeba', '君はいまやエリート集団の一員だ。', 'You are now among the elite.'),
	(104642, 122246, 'tatoeba', '日本人は集団で旅行するのが好きだ。', 'The Japanese like to travel in groups.'),
	(104643, 137723, 'tatoeba', '大きな集団の尻につくより頭になれ。', 'Better be the head of a cat than the tail of a lion.'),
	(104644, 111286, 'tatoeba', '彼はバスで登校する。', 'He goes to school by bus.'),
	(104645, 124606, 'tatoeba', '登校するところです。', 'I am going to school.'),
	(104646, 154908, 'tatoeba', '私は登校途中彼女にあった。', 'I met her along the way to school.'),
	(104647, 2207451, 'tatoeba', '彼は報告書を書いた。', 'He wrote the report.'),
	(104648, 10332779, 'tatoeba', '報告書は提出したの？', 'Have you turned in your report?'),
