	(124464, 183844, 'tatoeba', '管から水が吹き出した。', 'Water shot from the pipe.'),
	(124465, 994670, 'tatoeba', '下水管がつまっている。', 'The sewage pipe is obstructed.'),
	(124466, 9518947, 'tatoeba', '蛇口が水漏れしてるんです。', 'The faucet is leaking.'),
	(124467, 143823, 'tatoeba', '水が壊れた蛇口から吹き出した。', 'Water spouted from the broken faucet.'),
	(124468, 9676152, 'tatoeba', '僕の水筒、どこかな？', 'Where\'s my water bottle?'),
	(124469, 9676057, 'tatoeba', '僕の水筒、空っぽなんだけど。', 'My water bottle is empty.'),
	(124470, 143653, 'tatoeba', '水筒にはほとんど水が残っていない。', 'There is little water left in the canteen.'),
	(124471, 143654, 'tatoeba', '水虫が痛みます。', 'My athlete\'s foot hurts.'),
	(124472, 143656, 'tatoeba', '水虫がひどいのです。', 'I have bad athlete\'s foot.'),
	(124473, 143657, 'tatoeba', '水虫がかゆいのです。', 'I have athlete\'s foot and it\'s very itchy.'),
	(124474, 143663, 'tatoeba', '水増し決算の噂で株価は上がりませんでした。', 'The stock got creamed when they got wind of the dilution.'),
	(124475, 231278, 'tatoeba', 'あのパブではビールを水増ししているのではないか。', 'I suspect they water down the beer in that pub.'),
	(124476, 193404, 'tatoeba', 'もし論文の量が不足したら、引用文で水増ししておけばいい。', 'If your essay is on the short side, you can always pad it out with a few quotations.'),
	(124477, 175915, 'tatoeba', '決算報告を申し上げます。', 'We will now report on this year\'s business results.'),
	(124478, 211759, 'tatoeba', 'その会社は毎年３月に決算をする。', 'The company closes its books at the end of March.'),
	(124479, 11998584, 'tatoeba', '一緒に水族館に行かない？', 'Would you like to go to the aquarium with me?'),
	(124480, 10551241, 'tatoeba', '私、水族館初めてなんだ〜。', 'It\'s my first time coming to an aquarium.'),
	(124481, 143664, 'tatoeba', '水族館へ行く道を教えて頂けますか？', 'Can you show me the way to the aquarium?'),
	(124482, 9120207, 'tatoeba', '水槽を持ってるんだ。', 'I have a fish tank.'),
	(124483, 143665, 'tatoeba', '水槽にボウフラがうようよしている。', 'The water tank teems with mosquito larvae.'),
	(124484, 8924501, 'tatoeba', 'トムは水槽の魚を何時間も眺めていた。', 'Tom spent hours looking at the fish in the tank.'),
	(124485, 143669, 'tatoeba', '水先案内人は船を港に誘導する。', 'A pilot guides the ship toward the port.'),
	(124486, 143670, 'tatoeba', '水清ければ魚住まず。', 'Clear water breeds no fish.'),
	(124487, 145591, 'tatoeba', '心の清い人たちは幸いである。', 'Blessed are the pure in heart.'),
	(124488, 9032659, 'tatoeba', '清き一票をお願いします。', 'Please vote honestly.'),
	(124489, 3436314, 'tatoeba', '仮令遊女でも純粋な恋をすれば、その恋は無垢な清いものです。', 'Even if she\'s a prostitute which falls in love, her love is a pure and noble feeling.'),
	(124490, 203272, 'tatoeba', 'ダムの下流に水車小屋があった。', 'There was a water mill below the dam.'),
	(124491, 222338, 'tatoeba', 'この橋の上流に水車小屋がある。', 'There is a water mill above the bridge.'),
	(124492, 143671, 'tatoeba', '水車小屋は皆自分の水車に水を引く。', 'Every miller draws water to his own mill.'),
	(124493, 12035425, 'tatoeba', 'お花見に行こうよ。', 'Why don\'t we go and see the cherry blossoms?'),
	(124494, 8623887, 'tatoeba', '花見をしに来ました。', 'I came to look at the cherry blossoms.'),
	(124495, 227390, 'tatoeba', 'お花見に行きませんか？', 'Why don\'t we go and see the cherry blossoms?'),
	(124496, 143674, 'tatoeba', '水牛は牛に似ている。', 'A buffalo is akin to an ox.'),
	(124497, 229716, 'tatoeba', 'あれは牛ですか水牛ですか。', 'Is that a cow or a buffalo?'),
	(124498, 143675, 'tatoeba', '水牛は大きな角をもっている。', 'Buffaloes have big horns.'),
	(124499, 143676, 'tatoeba', '水割りにしてください。', 'I\'d like whiskey and water.'),
	(124500, 143677, 'tatoeba', '水割りをもう一杯ください。', 'Another Scotch and water, please.'),
	(124501, 11211633, 'tatoeba', 'ウィスキーの水割りをガッツリ飲んだ。', 'He slugged down a whiskey and water.'),
	(124502, 143678, 'tatoeba', '水害被災者たちは数校に収容された。', 'The flood victims were housed in several schools.'),
	(124503, 8914046, 'tatoeba', 'トムは水害保険に入ってないんだよ。', 'Tom doesn\'t have flood insurance.'),
	(124504, 185742, 'tatoeba', '我々は水害の被害者に食物と衣類を支給した。', 'We provided the flood victims with food and clothing.'),
	(124505, 143697, 'tatoeba', '水泳が次期オリンピックの主要競技となるだろう。', 'Swimming will be the main event of the next Olympics.'),
	(124506, 143710, 'tatoeba', '水を加え、練り粉がどろどろしない程度に混ぜなさい。', 'Add water and mix to a firm dough.'),
	(124507, 221067, 'tatoeba', 'この錠剤は何ですか。', 'What are these tablets?'),
	(124508, 146000, 'tatoeba', '錠剤のおかげで痛みがなくなった。', 'The tablets took away my pain.'),
	(124509, 143829, 'tatoeba', '水がなければこの錠剤は飲み込めません。', 'I can\'t swallow these tablets without a drink of water.'),
	(124510, 143759, 'tatoeba', '水は充分に加熱すると沸騰する。', 'Water will boil if heated enough.'),
	(124511, 10640395, 'tatoeba', '加熱した林檎にシュガーとシナモンを入れてね。', 'Add the sugar and cinnamon to the cooked apples.'),
	(124512, 143777, 'tatoeba', '水はセ氏100度で沸騰する。', 'Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius.'),
	(124513, 143783, 'tatoeba', '水は一滴も残っていない。', 'There is not a drop of water left.'),
	(124514, 10572040, 'tatoeba', '分かった。ほんの一滴ね。', 'OK, just a drop.'),
	(124515, 143788, 'tatoeba', '水の淀む所には汚物が溜る。', 'Standing pools gather filth.'),
	(124516, 210600, 'tatoeba', 'その国は鉱物資源に富んでいる。', 'That country is rich in minerals.'),
	(124517, 221262, 'tatoeba', 'この州には鉱物資源が豊富です。', 'The province is rich in mineral resources.'),
	(124518, 227795, 'tatoeba', 'オーストラリアは鉱物が豊富だ。', 'Australia is abundant in minerals.'),
	(124519, 143854, 'tatoeba', '吹き付ける冷たい風が骨身にしみた。', 'The icy wind cut us to the bones.'),
	(124520, 180539, 'tatoeba', '強い東風が我々の顔に激しく吹き付けた。', 'The strong east wind lashed at our faces.'),
	(124521, 143857, 'tatoeba', '図表２を見ると、これらの貿易サイクルのいくつかは非常に短期のものであることが判明する。', 'A glance at Chart 2 will reveal that some of these trade cycles are very short-lived.'),
	(124522, 10582925, 'tatoeba', '酢は嫌いです。', 'I don\'t like vinegar.'),
	(124523, 143895, 'tatoeba', '酢はすっぱい味がする。', 'Vinegar has a sharp taste.'),
	(124524, 10582928, 'tatoeba', 'お酢と油を持ってきてください。', 'Please bring me vinegar and oil.'),
	(124525, 143898, 'tatoeba', '陣痛が３０分おきに起こります。', 'I have labor pains every thirty minutes.'),
	(124526, 143900, 'tatoeba', '腎臓が悪いのです。', 'I have kidney trouble.'),
	(124527, 2760671, 'tatoeba', 'トムは腎臓と肝臓が悪い。', 'Tom\'s kidneys and liver are in bad shape.'),
	(124528, 212860, 'tatoeba', 'そのナイフは刃が鋭い。', 'The knife has a very sharp edge.'),
	(124529, 143904, 'tatoeba', '刃の鋭いナイフを手に入れた。', 'I\'ve got a keen-edged knife.'),
	(124530, 164140, 'tatoeba', '私のナイフの刃は、とても鋭い。', 'My knife has such a fine edge.'),
	(124531, 143908, 'tatoeba', '人類は太古の昔から指を用いて食べ物を食してきたのである。', 'People have eaten with their fingers from the beginning of history.'),
	(124532, 4900072, 'tatoeba', 'トムって究極に細かいよね。', 'Tom is extremely fussy.'),
	(124533, 180350, 'tatoeba', '教育の究極の目標とは何だろうか。', 'What is the ultimate purpose of education?'),
	(124534, 143920, 'tatoeba', '人類の究極的運命はどうなるであろうか。', 'What is man\'s ultimate destiny?'),
	(124535, 217851, 'tatoeba', 'これらの真珠は人造ではなく本物です。', 'These pearls are genuine, not artificial.'),
	(124536, 143944, 'tatoeba', '人前で彼を冷やかすなんて君は意地悪だ。', 'It is mean of you to ridicule him in public.'),
	(124537, 143957, 'tatoeba', '人生夢の如し。', 'Life is but an empty dream.'),
	(124538, 12976236, 'tatoeba', '人生は夢の如し。', 'Life is like a dream.'),
	(124539, 144743, 'tatoeba', '身を捨ててこそ浮かぶ瀬もあれ。', 'Risk all and gain all.'),
	(124540, 143958, 'tatoeba', '人生沈む瀬あれば浮かぶ瀬あるわけだから、あまりくよくよしないように。', 'Don\'t be so glum about it. Life has its ups and downs.'),
	(124541, 168575, 'tatoeba', '子供はその動物を面白がって眺めた。', 'The child watched the animal with amusement.'),
	(124542, 143972, 'tatoeba', '人生は面白おかしい事ばかりではない。', 'Life is not all beer and skittles.'),
	(124543, 210123, 'tatoeba', 'その子供は時計を面白がって分解した。', 'He took the clock apart just for fun.'),
	(124544, 163272, 'tatoeba', '私の心は空虚である。', 'My mind is a blank.'),
	(124545, 143984, 'tatoeba', '人生は空虚な夢ではない。', 'Life is not an empty dream.'),
	(124546, 144933, 'tatoeba', '神に向かって話しかけてみてもそこにあるのは空虚のみ。', 'I talk to God but the sky is empty.'),
	(124547, 143991, 'tatoeba', '人生は儚いよ、と人は言う。', 'People say that life is short.'),
	(124548, 143989, 'tatoeba', '人生は儚いよ、とよく人は言う。', 'They often say that life is short.'),
	(124549, 144007, 'tatoeba', '人生の無常をしみじみと感じる。', 'I feel the uncertainty of life.'),
	(124550, 144011, 'tatoeba', '人生の終局的な大きな目的は知識を獲得することではなくて行動することである。', 'The great end of life is not knowledge but action.'),
	(124551, 144021, 'tatoeba', '人生には浮き沈みがつきものだ。', 'Life is full of ups and downs.'),
	(124552, 330781, 'tatoeba', 'この国で、我々は一つの国として、一つの国民として浮き沈みをするのだ。', 'In this country, we rise or fall as one nation, as one people.'),
	(124553, 144047, 'tatoeba', '人生が不可解なものであることは私も認める。', 'That life is mysterious, I admit.'),
	(124554, 165882, 'tatoeba', '私たちは結婚を前提として交際しています。', 'We are dating with a view to marriage.'),
	(124555, 208386, 'tatoeba', 'その前提が妥当かどうかよく考えるべきだ。', 'You ought to think over whether the premise is valid or not.'),
	(124556, 144035, 'tatoeba', '人生とは不十分な前提から十分な結論を引き出す技術である。', 'Life is the art of drawing sufficient conclusions from insufficient premises.'),
	(124557, 12000649, 'tatoeba', 'もう後戻りはできないよ。', 'There\'s no turning back now.'),
	(124558, 144041, 'tatoeba', '人生という道で後戻りはできない。', 'There is no returning on the road of life.'),
	(124559, 194484, 'tatoeba', 'もうここまで来たらやるしかないでしょう。もう後戻りはできない。', 'We\'ve come this far, so we can\'t stop now. I don\'t want to backslide.'),
	(124560, 144049, 'tatoeba', '人生から非常な喜びを感ずる。', 'I get a kick out of life.'),
	(124561, 1328060, 'tatoeba', '私が本当の母親ではないことを娘は薄々感ずいているようだ。', 'It seems as if my daughter is faintly aware that I\'m not her real mother.'),
	(124562, 144061, 'tatoeba', '人々は噴火で大損害を受けた。', 'People suffered heavy losses in the eruptions.'),
	(124563, 211958, 'tatoeba', 'その火山は今年２度噴火した。', 'The volcano has erupted twice this year.'),
	(124564, 209471, 'tatoeba', 'その種は火山の噴火後、衰えた。', 'After the volcanic eruption, this species declined.'),
	(124565, 144076, 'tatoeba', '人々は彼の突然の死を深く悼んだ。', 'People regretted his sudden death deeply.'),
	(124566, 144078, 'tatoeba', '人々は都会の炎熱を避けようとする。', 'People seek escape from the heat of the town.'),
	(124567, 144096, 'tatoeba', '人々は侵略を撃退することができた。', 'The people could repel the invasion.'),
	(124568, 213535, 'tatoeba', 'そして、賃金として得た代用貨幣はその店でしか使えませんでした。', 'And the tokens he received as wages could only be spent at that shop.'),
	(124569, 144138, 'tatoeba', '人々はパレードを見ようと沿道に集まった。', 'People amassed along the streets to watch the parade.'),
	(124570, 144146, 'tatoeba', '人々はその孤児を哀れんだ。', 'People took pity on the orphan.'),
	(124571, 148251, 'tatoeba', '宗教は、自暴自棄になった移民達を哀れんで助けを与えた。', 'The bishop took pity on the desperate immigrants.'),
	(124572, 147436, 'tatoeba', '渚に人が群がっていた。', 'There were flocks of people on the beach.'),
	(124573, 211977, 'tatoeba', 'その歌手はファンの群がる中を苦心して進んだ。', 'The singer fought his way through the crowd of fans.'),
	(124574, 9241027, 'tatoeba', '俺たちの周りに人が群がったんだ。', 'People gathered around us.'),
	(124575, 225323, 'tatoeba', 'ケーキにアリの大群が群がっていた。', 'There was an army of ants at the cake.'),
	(124576, 176697, 'tatoeba', '群集が大統領を見送りに空港に群がった。', 'The crowd gathered at the airport to see the President off.'),
	(124577, 144155, 'tatoeba', '人々はケガ人の回りに群がっていたが、医者が事故現場に着くと道をあけた。', 'The people crowded round the injured man, but they made way for the doctor when he reached the scene of the accident.'),
	(124578, 2764096, 'tatoeba', 'この付近は駐車禁止です。', 'You can\'t park around here.'),
	(124579, 144175, 'tatoeba', '人々が浜辺付近で遊んでいる。', 'People are playing near the beach.'),
	(124580, 220087, 'tatoeba', 'この付近はモダンな建物が多い。', 'There are many modern buildings around here.'),
	(124581, 144250, 'tatoeba', '人間は複雑な有機体だ。', 'Man is a complex organism.'),
	(124582, 183345, 'tatoeba', '機体が揺れ始めて乗客は不安になった。', 'Passengers became nervous when the plane began to vibrate.'),
	(124583, 144255, 'tatoeba', '人間は鋳型に入れて作るわけにはいかない。', 'A man cannot be made in a mold.'),
	(124584, 170230, 'tatoeba', '罪人は絞首台に送られた。', 'The criminal was sent to the gallows.'),
	(124585, 170229, 'tatoeba', '罪人は考えを変えるよう彼に懇願した。', 'The criminal pleaded with him to change his mind.'),
	(124586, 144338, 'tatoeba', '人間の野蛮性は決して根絶できない。', 'The savage in man is never quite eradicated.'),
	(124587, 10637246, 'tatoeba', '最近、物欲がわかなくてね。', 'I haven\'t had the desire for stuff lately.'),
	(124588, 144340, 'tatoeba', '人間の物欲はその収入が増すにつれて大きくなる。', 'Men\'s wants become greater in proportion to the increase in their income.'),
	(124589, 144348, 'tatoeba', '人間の真理の探究に対して不朽の貢献をした書物を、我々は偉大な書物と呼ぶのである。', 'Those books which have made a lasting contribution to man\'s quest for truth, we call great books.'),
	(124590, 220957, 'tatoeba', 'この数年間に彼は不朽の名詩を書いた。', 'During these years he wrote immortal poems.'),
	(124591, 222919, 'tatoeba', 'この映画はまさしく不朽の名作である。', 'This film is indeed an enduring masterpiece.'),
	(124592, 179729, 'tatoeba', '金は諸悪の根源。', 'Money is the root of all evil.'),
	(124593, 991871, 'tatoeba', '貧乏は諸悪の根源。', 'Poverty is the root of all evil.'),
	(124594, 174207, 'tatoeba', '誤解を正させてください。', 'Please let me set the record straight.'),
	(124595, 193740, 'tatoeba', 'もし間違っていたら正して下さい。', 'Correct me if I am wrong.'),
	(124596, 174206, 'tatoeba', '誤解を正してくださってありがとう。', 'Thank you for setting the record straight.'),
	(124597, 177821, 'tatoeba', '君はこれからの誤りを正さなければならない。', 'You must put these mistakes right.'),
	(124598, 144440, 'tatoeba', '人は不正を正したいときは法律に頼ることが出来る。', 'People can turn to the law if they want to correct an injustice.'),
	(124599, 146017, 'tatoeba', '状況をただちに正していただけるようお願いします。', 'I hope you will correct the situation immediately.'),
	(124600, 144499, 'tatoeba', '人は互いの家を詳しく調べるのが大好きだ。', 'People love to inspect each other\'s houses.'),
	(124601, 177749, 'tatoeba', '君はその結果を甘受すべきだ。', 'You should abide by the consequences.'),
	(124602, 144528, 'tatoeba', '人は運命を甘受せざるを得ない。', 'One can\'t quarrel with destiny.'),
	(124603, 1568244, 'tatoeba', '私たちは自分が選択した結果を甘受しなければならない。', 'We have to live with the consequences of our choices.'),
	(124604, 10914828, 'tatoeba', 'お言葉に甘えるね。', 'If you insist.'),
	(124605, 8606829, 'tatoeba', 'じゃあ、お言葉に甘えて。', 'I\'ll take you up on that.'),
	(124606, 10522615, 'tatoeba', '彼女に甘えられると弱いんだ。', 'She makes me melt when she pampers me.'),
	(124607, 8606821, 'tatoeba', 'お言葉に甘えさせていただきます。', 'I\'ll take you up on that.'),
	(124608, 217109, 'tatoeba', 'ご親切に甘えているようで気掛かりです。', 'I\'m afraid I\'m imposing on your hospitality.'),
	(124609, 210178, 'tatoeba', 'その子は母親に甘えた。', 'The child played the baby to his mother.'),
	(124610, 144666, 'tatoeba', '人には、迷いと苦しみのもとである煩悩がある。', 'People have worldly passions which lead them into delusions and sufferings.'),
	(124611, 220156, 'tatoeba', 'この煩悩のきずなから逃れるには五つの方法がある。', 'There are five ways to emancipate themselves from the bond of worldly passions.'),
	(124612, 144708, 'tatoeba', '進退きわまった。', 'I am in a tight place.'),
	(124613, 186961, 'tatoeba', '家主に家賃を払えば、食物を買う金がなくなる。進退きわまったというところだ。', 'If we pay the rent to the landlady, we won\'t have any money for food; we are between the devil and the deep blue sea.'),
	(124614, 147747, 'tatoeba', '出処進退の潔さをわきまえている、と彼は言っているけれど、いざとなったらどうだかね。', 'He always talks as though he knows how to handle himself but you never know how he\'ll act when the chips are down.'),
	(124615, 144723, 'tatoeba', '辛口がほしいのですが。', 'I want something dry.'),
	(124616, 11725528, 'tatoeba', '僕は辛口カレーが好きなんだ。', 'I like hot curry.'),
	(124617, 11013784, 'tatoeba', '点数高いけど辛口なアドバイスだった。', 'I got a high score, but the advice was harsh.'),
	(124618, 205984, 'tatoeba', 'そもそも事故の大半は熱帯雨林ではなく、身近な場所でおこるのである。', 'Most accidents, after all, happen around the corner, not in the rainforest.'),
	(124619, 144781, 'tatoeba', '親族達は彼の無罪を確信していた。', 'His relatives were convinced of his innocence.'),
	(124620, 163250, 'tatoeba', '私の親族は皆この町に住んでいる。', 'All my relatives live in this city.'),
	(124621, 9474633, 'tatoeba', '海外にご親族はいらっしゃいますか？', 'Do you have relatives abroad?'),
	(124622, 144785, 'tatoeba', '親切は１つの美学である。', 'Kindness is a virtue.'),
	(124623, 182865, 'tatoeba', '議論の多くの個所で、アドルノ、ホルクハイマーらの美学論に恩恵を受けている。', 'My argument is indebted in a number of places to the aesthetic theories of Adorno, Horkheimer and others.'),
	(124624, 144801, 'tatoeba', '親孝行したいときには親はなし。', 'By the time you wish to be a good son, your parents are long gone.'),
